WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:16.321
By late afternoon things were almost settled.

2
00:00:17.302 --> 00:00:19.443
Daisy was at Grace's house with Kaleem.

3
00:00:20.703 --> 00:00:22.604
Beatrice was on her headband.

4
00:00:22.624 --> 00:00:25.485
"I just called Mrs.

5
00:00:25.545 --> 00:00:27.746
Ortiz," Grace's mom announced.

6
00:00:28.466 --> 00:00:29.867
"Scamp can stay with us."

7
00:00:30.847 --> 00:00:31.828
The kids cheered.

8
00:00:33.676 --> 00:00:36.838
"Thanks for the great idea, Daisy," Grace said.

9
00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:38.459
Daisy nodded.

10
00:00:39.919 --> 00:00:41.380
Then she whispered to Kaleem.

11
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.541
"Distract Grace for a second.

12
00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:45.763
I want to explain things to the fish."

13
00:00:49.265 --> 00:00:52.587
Once they were gone, Daisy stepped over to the fish tank.

14
00:00:56.849 --> 00:00:58.750
fish. You're going to be moving."

15
00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:01.892
"To a new tank?"

16
00:01:02.676 --> 00:01:04.497
a fish asked, sounding bored.

17
00:01:04.517 --> 00:01:08.178
"No, your whole tank is moving to a new place."

18
00:01:09.158 --> 00:01:10.118
Daisy smiled.

19
00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:11.659
"You see, Mrs.

20
00:01:11.759 --> 00:01:13.279
Ortiz can't keep Scamp.

21
00:01:13.559 --> 00:01:20.241
But she still wants—" "You talk about humans all the time," another fish said.

22
00:01:20.261 --> 00:01:24.903
"You should talk about us—and admire our beauty."

23
00:01:26.323 --> 00:01:27.123
Daisy giggled.

24
00:01:27.143 --> 00:01:29.164
"That's what I'm trying to tell you.

25
00:01:29.716 --> 00:01:32.558
Soon you'll have someone admiring you all day long.

26
00:01:33.658 --> 00:01:34.659
You're moving with Mrs.

27
00:01:34.739 --> 00:01:36.540
Ortiz to her son's condo.

28
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.702
She's not allowed to have a dog there, but fish are just fine."

29
00:01:40.722 --> 00:01:44.344
"Naturally," a fish said.

30
00:01:44.364 --> 00:01:47.987
"Fish are the only truly excellent creatures."

31
00:01:49.387 --> 00:01:52.249
Beatrice buzzed in a way that sounded like a snort.

32
00:01:52.269 --> 00:01:56.051
"Fish aren't that great," she muttered.

33
00:01:57.484 --> 00:02:01.147
"Anyway, with your tank gone, Scamp can live here," Daisy said.

34
00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:04.070
"He'll be moving in as soon as you're gone.

35
00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.111
Now everyone is happy."

36
00:02:09.614 --> 00:02:11.596
Beatrice cheered in Daisy's ear.

37
00:02:11.616 --> 00:02:14.158
"You did it, Daisy!

38
00:02:14.538 --> 00:02:20.383
I knew you could—" Beatrice suddenly felt an odd tug, and then Poof!

39
00:02:25.184 --> 00:02:29.287
The bumblebee found herself back on the rocky beach with the Council of Animals.

40
00:02:30.408 --> 00:02:31.529
Beatrice shook her head.

41
00:02:36.352 --> 00:02:37.733
it already been a week?

42
00:02:38.554 --> 00:02:39.774
Is that why I'm back?"

43
00:02:41.195 --> 00:02:42.256
The elephant nodded.

44
00:02:42.276 --> 00:02:46.659
"What news do you have about our young ambassador?"

45
00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:49.461
Beatrice thought for a moment.

46
00:02:49.481 --> 00:02:52.804
"Well, Daisy loves talking with animals.

47
00:02:53.756 --> 00:02:55.297
She's helped many already."

48
00:02:56.358 --> 00:03:01.221
Beatrice told the council about Scamp, Floyd, and all of Daisy's other adventures.

49
00:03:01.241 --> 00:03:04.664
"So she's doing well," the pig said.

50
00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:07.006
"Have there been any problems?"

51
00:03:08.026 --> 00:03:09.127
Beatrice hesitated.

52
00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:11.289
"Perhaps one problem.

53
00:03:12.349 --> 00:03:14.811
She told her best friend about her new ability."

54
00:03:14.831 --> 00:03:17.613
"What?" the magpie cried.

55
00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:19.955
Beatrice buzzed nervously.

56
00:03:19.975 --> 00:03:21.236
"I'm sorry.

57
00:03:21.708 --> 00:03:24.851
I think it was my fault for not being clear with her."

58
00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:28.534
"This is a grave problem."

59
00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:30.275
The elephant looked upset.

60
00:03:30.796 --> 00:03:33.898
"Were there any other issues we should know about?"

61
00:03:33.918 --> 00:03:38.642
"She almost told a few other people," Beatrice said.

62
00:03:38.662 --> 00:03:40.844
"But she didn't in the end!

63
00:03:41.765 --> 00:03:44.567
And she almost gave up when she couldn't find a home for Scamp.

64
00:03:45.047 --> 00:03:47.529
But then she figured out how to help him."

65
00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.232
The council members exchanged looks.

66
00:03:51.628 --> 00:03:54.251
"Hmm," the sea turtle said.

67
00:03:54.271 --> 00:03:59.815
"I suppose we can continue the experiment—at least for now."

68
00:03:59.835 --> 00:04:02.077
"F-for now?"

69
00:04:02.457 --> 00:04:03.238
Beatrice said.

70
00:04:03.258 --> 00:04:04.699
"What do you mean?"

71
00:04:04.719 --> 00:04:10.804
"If the human ambassador makes too many mistakes, we'll have to remove her gift."

72
00:04:11.565 --> 00:04:12.966
The elephant lifted her trunk.

73
00:04:13.506 --> 00:04:16.829
"We'll bring you back in due time for another report."

74
00:04:16.849 --> 00:04:20.372
"Good luck, little bee," the magpie said.

75
00:04:21.004 --> 00:04:26.551
"We're counting on you and your young human friend.

76
00:04:27.032 --> 00:04:27.913
What's her name again?"

77
00:04:32.079 --> 00:04:35.323
Beatrice said, preparing to be magically transported again.

78
00:04:35.343 --> 00:04:36.424
"Daisy
